@startuml

title The workflow definition and its step definitions

class "workflow definition\n(registered code)" as def <<definition>> #E1F5FF {
    {field} +type name : name
    {field} +description : text
    {field} +failure policy : compensate | stop-and-retry
    {field} +build steps : function(request, tenant, correlation)
}

class "step definition" as step <<definition>> #E1F5FF {
    {field} +name : name
    {field} +description : text
    {field} +command subject : subject
    {field} +compensation subject : subject, or none
    {field} +build command : function(request, results)
    {field} +build compensation : function(command, result)
}

class "materialised step\n(persisted on the run)" as mat <<state>> #FFF4E1 {
    {field} +name : name
    {field} +command subject : subject
    {field} +compensation subject : subject
}

def "1" --> "*" step : builds once per run
step ..> mat : resolved into

note bottom of def
    The type name is the interface: the key in
    the registry, the value the start message
    carries, and the value the run stores.
end note

note bottom of mat
    Persisted at start and never rebuilt, so
    a restart or a deployment does not reshape
    a run that is in progress.
end note

@enduml
